  "notes": "⚠ **`low`, and the research says why.** It is rated medium-low: the chart, the label and a complete 14-producer board across 16 tracks are sourced, but *no interview establishes his own workflow*, so **every drum and harmonic number here is genre-plus-board inference** — `kick`, `hihat`, `percs`, `snareRoll` and the extensions are all INFERRED, and the only sourced parameters are the tempo band, the key set and the arrangement. Even the tempo carries a `[LOW-CONF]` mark, because readings at 144–187 fold in half onto 72–94. What is modellable is the *board*, and that is the reason the entry exists: a Shady-camp-plus-West-Coast-journeyman bench (Domingo, Sha Money XL, Punch, Focus…, Ron Browz, Havoc, DJ Khalil, Sam Sneed, Megahertz, J.R. Rotem, Eminem with Jeff Bass and Luis Resto) rather than the Dr. Dre / Scott Storch board the existing `50 Cent / G-Unit era` entry models — which is why he is not absorbed into it. The parameters that carry it: **a clap over the snare with the widest offset in this batch**, a 2005 Interscope 8th-hat kit with 16th accents, **a sustained sub separated from the kick by envelope rather than pitch and no slides at all** (`glideProb` 0, `followRootsProb` 0.95), Phrygian synth leads over 2-bar static `i` vamps, and `i–VI–VII` where there is motion at all. The melodic movement is supplied by R&B guest hooks rather than the beat, so `densityPerBar` is low and the countermelody is the loudest melodic department here.",
